// # Net Transport
//
// Logline: Telecom + DSP + PHY-layer transport codecs. Phase 3.3 reorg: merged
// the prior std/net/telecom/, std/net/telecom_5g/, std/net/telecom_6g/ into a
// single std/net/transport/ tree. The 3G/4G/5G/6G distinctions are preserved
// at the file naming layer (telecom_5g_*, telecom_6g_*, thz_*, ris_*, isac_*,
// nr5g_*, lte_*, holographic_*, otfs_*, ofdm_*, sdr_*, sync_*) but the
// directory split is gone -- they were distinctions without a difference.
//
// Setup: Domain module under std/net/transport. Pure compute, no caps.
//   * Legacy telecom/ surface: beamforming, channel, CRC, DSP filters, FFT/IFFT, LTE, NR5G frame/slot/subcarrier, OFDM, modulators, SDR, SNR, turbo/viterbi, spectrum.
//   * 5G surface: 3GPP channels, advanced DSP, MIMO, mod constellations, NR5G LDPC/polar/rate-match, OFDM cyclic prefix/papr/pilot, SDR, sync.
//   * 6G surface: holographic MIMO, OAM, OTFS, RIS, semantic comms, terahertz, ISAC, RSMA, GFDM, FBMC, lens antenna, near-field, mMIMO, NOMA.
//
// Beats:
//   1. Legacy telecom (25 files): the original std/net/telecom/ public surface.
//   2. 5G NR + advanced DSP + MIMO + OFDM + sync (50 files): the std/net/telecom_5g/ surface.
//   3. 6G + terahertz + RIS + ISAC + near-field (50 files): the std/net/telecom_6g/ surface.

